# FHIR-12 — MidSizedClinic Imaging Workflow (Mandatory)

Clinical workflow rules for MidSizedClinic ultrasound operations. Source of truth: [clinic-workflow.md](../skills/product-owner-overview/clinic-workflow.md). Stacks with **FHIR-10**, **FHIR-11**, **FHIR-00**, **FHIR-01**.

Workflow violations break **audit trail**, **role separation**, and **study→report chain of custody**.

## Actors & Sequence

```
Reception/Tech          Radiologist           Integration/Referrer
      │                       │                        │
      ├─ Search prior studies (FHIR-11)                  │
      ├─ POST ImagingStudy (capture)                    │
      │                       ├─ GET ImagingStudy/{id} │
      │                       ├─ POST DiagnosticReport  │
      │                       │                        ├─ GET DiagnosticReport
      └─ (audit logged)       └─ (audit logged)         └─ delivery < 5 min SLA
```

## 1. Technician Workflow — Capture Study

**Actor:** `clinicTechnician` — steps 1–2 in clinic-workflow.md

- **ALWAYS** create studies via `POST /ImagingStudy` after capture (step 2: Technician Captures New Ultrasound).
- **MUST** set `ImagingStudy.status` to **`available`** on successful capture POST — study is ready for radiologist review.
- **MUST** set `ImagingStudy.modality` (e.g. `US` for ultrasound) and `started` at capture time.
- **MUST** set `ImagingStudy.subject` → `Patient/{id}`.
- **NEVER** set `DiagnosticReport` status or create reports — **technicians CANNOT create DiagnosticReport** (403 + `OperationOutcome`).
- **NEVER** skip from scheduled intake to `appended` without radiologist report.

```http
# ✅ RIGHT — technician capture (clinic-workflow step 2)
POST /ImagingStudy
{
  "resourceType": "ImagingStudy",
  "status": "available",
  "modality": [{ "system": "http://dicom.nema.org/resources/ontology/DCM", "code": "US" }],
  "subject": { "reference": "Patient/pat-1001" },
  "started": "2026-08-11T14:30:00Z",
  "description": "Abdominal ultrasound — routine"
}

# ❌ WRONG — technician creates report
POST /DiagnosticReport   ← FORBIDDEN for clinicTechnician role
```

**If violated:** radiologist queue empty or wrong; scope-of-practice breach; audit shows tech authoring clinical reports.

## 2. Radiologist Workflow — Read Then Report

**Actor:** `clinicRadiologist` — step 3 in clinic-workflow.md

- **ALWAYS** read the study before authoring: `GET /ImagingStudy/{id}` (PACS review is external; FHIR holds metadata + linkage).
- **MUST** create report via `POST /DiagnosticReport` only **after** study exists with `status=available`.
- **MUST** link report to study (see §3) and set initial `DiagnosticReport.status` to **`preliminary`** while drafting.
- **MUST** transition to **`final`** on sign-out (radiologist `Practitioner` reference + `issued` timestamp).
- **NEVER** create or update ImagingStudy — **radiologists CANNOT create ImagingStudy** (403 + `OperationOutcome`).

```http
# ✅ RIGHT — radiologist flow (clinic-workflow step 3)
GET /ImagingStudy/stu-2001

POST /DiagnosticReport
{
  "resourceType": "DiagnosticReport",
  "status": "preliminary",
  "subject": { "reference": "Patient/pat-1001" },
  "basedOn": [{ "reference": "ImagingStudy/stu-2001" }],
  "conclusion": "No acute findings."
}
```

**If violated:** unsigned reports in production; imaging metadata altered by non-capture role; audit cannot prove read-before-write.

## 3. Report Delivery — Linkage Required

**Actor:** Integration / clinic staff — step 4 in clinic-workflow.md

- **MUST** link every DiagnosticReport to its ImagingStudy via **`basedOn`** → `ImagingStudy/{id}` **OR** valid **`study`** reference (prefer `basedOn` for new writes).
- **MUST** set `DiagnosticReport.subject` → same `Patient/{id}` as the linked ImagingStudy.
- **ALWAYS** serve delivery queries as standard FHIR reads: `GET /DiagnosticReport/{id}`, `GET /Patient/{id}`, `GET /ImagingStudy/{id}`.
- **NEVER** deliver a report bundle where DiagnosticReport cannot be resolved to exactly one ImagingStudy.

**If violated:** referrer EHR cannot reconcile report to study; step 4 delivery fails SLA; compliance chain-of-custody breaks.

## 4. Status Transitions — Allowed Paths Only

### ImagingStudy

```
requested ──(tech POST capture)──► available ──(report final)──► appended
   │                                   │
   └──────── cancelled (admin only) ───┴──────── cancelled
```

| From | To | Who | Trigger |
|---|---|---|---|
| `requested` | `available` | Technician | `POST /ImagingStudy` after capture |
| `available` | `appended` | System/radiologist sign-out | DiagnosticReport → `final` linked to study |
| `*` | `cancelled` | Clinic admin only | Audited cancel; not technician/radiologist default |

- **MUST NOT** jump `requested` → `appended` without `available` and a `final` report.
- **MUST NOT** revert `appended` → `available` without admin audit path.

### DiagnosticReport

```
preliminary ──(radiologist sign-out)──► final
     │                                      │
     └──────── cancelled ───────────────────┴── amended (correction path)
```

- **MUST** start at `preliminary` on `POST`; **MUST** end at `final` before referrer delivery (clinic-workflow step 4).
- **NEVER** deliver `preliminary` reports to referring providers.

**If violated:** worklist shows wrong queue state; premature delivery of unsigned reports; monthly compliance audit fails.

## 5. Role Enforcement — Hard Boundaries

From clinic-workflow.md roles table — enforce in handlers before any work (FHIR-00):

| Role | ImagingStudy | DiagnosticReport |
|---|---|---|
| **Technician** | CREATE, READ, UPDATE status (capture path only) | READ only |
| **Radiologist** | READ only | CREATE, READ, UPDATE (preliminary→final) |
| **Clinic admin** | DELETE/cancel (audit-logged) | — |

- **Technicians CANNOT** `POST`/`PUT` DiagnosticReport — **NEVER** bypass with shared `globalWriter` in production clinic config.
- **Radiologists CANNOT** `POST`/`PUT` ImagingStudy — capture is technician-owned.
- **MUST** log user, role, resource ID, and action on every transition (FHIR-01 audit context).

**If violated:** HIPAA minimum-necessary failure; monthly audit (clinic-workflow step 5) flags unauthorized actor; role separation lawsuit exposure.

---

## Forbidden — Do Not Generate

| Forbidden | Consequence |
|---|---|
| Technician `POST /DiagnosticReport` | Scope-of-practice + audit failure |
| Radiologist `POST /ImagingStudy` | Capture integrity broken |
| Report without `basedOn`/study link | Delivery/interop failure |
| `DiagnosticReport.final` before `GET` study path | No read-before-write proof |
| Deliver `preliminary` to referrer | Unsigned report in EHR |
| ImagingStudy `appended` without `final` report | False "reported" state |
| Status skip `requested` → `appended` | Broken workflow + worklist |
| Shared super-user role for tech and rad | Role separation collapse |

Implement workflow guards in **handlers**, not UI-only checks. **MUST** cover technician/radiologist forbidden paths in unit tests and happy-path in E2E.
